  "term": "psychedelic therapy",
  "definition": "Psychedelic therapy is a therapeutic approach that uses psychedelic substances as part of treatment for psychiatric disorders. The packet describes it as an emerging area supported by clinical trial evidence, especially for difficult-to-treat conditions such as PTSD and depression.",
